  "body": "Follow-up to #128. `camcraft-cli mcp` drives its own headless document. The issue also asks for a live connection to a running app, so the user can watch the agent work in the viewport.\n\nWanted: the GUI hosts the same tool table (`app::mcp`) over a local transport (stdio bridge or localhost streamable HTTP). Tool calls are queued onto the UI's pending command queue, so they run on the UI thread through the app's own History, and undo in the app undoes the agent's steps.\n\nDone means: an agent connected to a running app adds an operation, the browser shows it, and Ctrl+Z removes it.\n",
